      "text": "157, 325.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 571 by 5, which gives me 2,855.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 571 by 70, resulting in 39,970.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 571 by 200, which equals 114,200.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 2,855 + 39,970 + 114,200.\n\nAdding them up, I get 157,025.\n\nSo, the correct product of 571 and 275 is 157,025.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 571 and 275 is \\boxed{157025}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 571 and 275, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 571 by 5 (the ones place of 275):**\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 5 = 2,855\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 571 by 70 (the tens place of 275):**\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 70 = 39,970\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 571 by 200 (the hundreds place of 275):**\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 200 = 114,200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   2,855 + 39,970 + 114,200 = 157,025\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of 571 and 275 is \\boxed{157025}.",
