      "text": "343,  343.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 397 by 8 (the ones place of 868):\n\n397 \u00d7 8 = 3,176\n\nNext, I'll multiply 397 by 60 (the tens place of 868):\n\n397 \u00d7 60 = 23,820\n\nThen, I'll multiply 397 by 800 (the hundreds place of 868):\n\n397 \u00d7 800 = 317,600\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together:\n\n3,176 + 23,820 = 26,996\n\n26,996 + 317,600 = 344,596\n\nSo, the final product of 397 and 868 is 344,596.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 397 and 868 is \\boxed{344596}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 397 and 868, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 397 by 8 (the ones place of 868):**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 8 = 3,176\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 397 by 60 (the tens place of 868):**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 60 = 23,820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 397 by 800 (the hundreds place of 868):**\n   \\[\n   397 \\times 800 = 317,600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   3,176 + 23,820 + 317,600 = 344,596\n   \\]\n\nSo, the final product of 397 and 868 is \\(\\boxed{344596}\\).",
