      "index": 0,
      "text": "123, 123.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 217 by 8, which gives me 1,736.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 217 by 60, resulting in 13,020.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 217 by 500, which equals 108,500.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 1,736 + 13,020 + 108,500.\n\nAdding them up, I get 123,256.\n\nSo, the correct product of 217 and 568 is 123,256.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 217 and 568 is \\boxed{123256}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 217 and 568, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 217 by 8 (the ones place of 568):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 8 = 1,736\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 217 by 60 (the tens place of 568):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 60 = 13,020\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 217 by 500 (the hundreds place of 568):**\n   \\[\n   217 \\times 500 = 108,500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1,736 + 13,020 + 108,500 = 123,256\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of 217 and 568 is \\boxed{123256}.",
