      "text": "224, 248.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 666 by 8, which gives me 5,328.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 666 by 30, resulting in 19,980.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 666 by 300, which equals 199,800.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 5,328 + 19,980 + 199,800 equals 225,108.\n\nSo, the correct product of 666 and 338 is 225,108.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 666 and 338 is \\boxed{225108}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 666 and 338, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 666 by 8 (the ones place of 338):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 8 = 5328\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 666 by 30 (the tens place of 338):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 30 = 19980\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 666 by 300 (the hundreds place of 338):**\n   \\[\n   666 \\times 300 = 199800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   5328 + 19980 + 199800 = 225108\n   \\]\n\nSo, the product of 666 and 338 is \\(\\boxed{225108}\\).",
