      "text": "65,178.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 174 by 4 (ones place of 374):**\n   - 4 \u00d7 4 = 16. Write down 6 and carry over 1.\n   - 4 \u00d7 7 = 28, plus the carried 1 equals 29. Write down 9 and carry over 2.\n   - 4 \u00d7 1 = 4, plus the carried 2 equals 6.\n   - **Partial Product:** 696\n\n2. **Multiply 174 by 70 (tens place of 374):**\n   - 70 \u00d7 4 = 280. Write down 0 and carry over 28.\n   - 70 \u00d7 7 = 490, plus the carried 28 equals 518. Write down 8 and carry over 51.\n   - 70 \u00d7 1 = 70, plus the carried 51 equals 121.\n   - **Partial Product:** 12,180\n\n3. **Multiply 174 by 300 (hundreds place of 374):**\n   - 300 \u00d7 4 = 1,200. Write down 00 and carry over 12.\n   - 300 \u00d7 7 = 2,100, plus the carried 12 equals 2,112. Write down 12 and carry over 21.\n   - 300 \u00d7 1 = 300, plus the carried 21 equals 321.\n   - **Partial Product:** 52,200\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - 696 + 12,180 + 52,200 = 65,178\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 174 and 374 is \\boxed{65178}.",
