      "index": 0,
      "text": "91,054.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 347 by 2 (units place of 262):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 2 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n   - 4 \u00d7 2 = 8, plus the carried 1 equals 9.\n   - 3 \u00d7 2 = 6.\n   - **Partial Product:** 694\n\n2. **Multiply 347 by 60 (tens place of 262):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 6 = 42. Write down 2 and carry over 4.\n   - 4 \u00d7 6 = 24, plus the carried 4 equals 28. Write down 8 and carry over 2.\n   - 3 \u00d7 6 = 18, plus the carried 2 equals 20.\n   - **Partial Product:** 20,820\n\n3. **Multiply 347 by 200 (hundreds place of 262):**\n   - 7 \u00d7 2 = 14. Write down 4 and carry over 1.\n   - 4 \u00d7 2 = 8, plus the carried 1 equals 9.\n   - 3 \u00d7 2 = 6.\n   - **Partial Product:** 69,400\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   - 694 + 20,820 + 69,400 = 91,054\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 347 and 262 is \\boxed{91054}.",
