      "text": "235,512.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 662 by 6 (ones place of 356):**\n   - 6 \u00d7 2 = 12. Write down 2 and carry over 1.\n   - 6 \u00d7 6 = 36, plus the carried 1 equals 37. Write down 7 and carry over 3.\n   - 6 \u00d7 6 = 36, plus the carried 3 equals 39. Write down 39.\n   - **Partial Product:** 3,972\n\n2. **Multiply 662 by 50 (tens place of 356):**\n   - 50 \u00d7 2 = 100. Write down 00 and carry over 10.\n   - 50 \u00d7 6 = 300, plus the carried 10 equals 310. Write down 10 and carry over 31.\n   - 50 \u00d7 6 = 300, plus the carried 31 equals 331. Write down 331.\n   - **Partial Product:** 33,100\n\n3. **Multiply 662 by 300 (hundreds place of 356):**\n   - 300 \u00d7 2 = 600. Write down 00 and carry over 60.\n   - 300 \u00d7 6 = 1,800, plus the carried 60 equals 1,860. Write down 60 and carry over 186.\n   - 300 \u00d7 6 = 1,800, plus the carried 186 equals 1,986. Write down 1,986.\n   - **Partial Product:** 198,600\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - 3,972 + 33,100 + 198,600 = 235,512\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 662 and 356 is \\boxed{235512}.",
