      "text": "890, 126.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 916 by 1, which gives me 916.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 916 by 70, resulting in 64,120.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 916 by 900, which equals 824,400.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 916 + 64,120 + 824,400.\n\nAdding them up, I get 890, 126.\n\nHmm, that still doesn't look correct. I must have made a mistake in my calculations. Let me check each step again.\n\nAfter rechecking, I realize that the correct sum should be 890, 126.\n\nWait, that still doesn't seem accurate. I think I need to approach this differently.\n\nLet me try multiplying 916 by 971 directly.\n\nMultiplying 916 by 971 gives me 890, 126.\n\nNo, that's not right either. I must have made an error in my multiplication.\n\nI think I need to break it down further. Let me try multiplying 916 by 900, which is 824,400.\n\nThen, multiply 916 by 70, resulting in 64,120.\n\nNext, multiply 916 by 1, giving me 916.\n\nNow, adding all these together: 824,400 + 64,120 + 916.\n\nAdding 824,400 and 64,120 gives me 888,520.\n\nAdding 916 to that, I get 889,436.\n\nWait, that's different from before. I think I made a mistake in my initial addition.\n\nLet me verify the addition step by step.\n\n824,400 plus 64,120 is 888,520.\n\nAdding 916 to 888,520 gives me 889,436.\n\nYes, that seems correct now.\n\nSo, the final product of 916 and 971 is 889,436.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 916 and 971 is \\boxed{889436}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 916 and 971, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps:\n\n1. Multiply 916 by 1 (the ones place of 971):\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 1 = 916\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 916 by 70 (the tens place of 971):\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 70 = 64,120\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 916 by 900 (the hundreds place of 971):\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 900 = 824,400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add all the partial products together:\n\\[\n916 + 64,120 + 824,400 = 889,436\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 916 and 971 is \\(\\boxed{889436}\\).",
