      "index": 0,
      "text": "174,080.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Set Up the Multiplication:**\n   ```\n     640\n   \u00d7 272\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 640 by 2 (units place):**\n   ```\n     640\n   \u00d7   2\n   ----\n    1280\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply 640 by 70 (tens place):**\n   - Multiply 640 by 7: 640 \u00d7 7 = 4,480\n   - Add a zero for the tens place: 4,4800\n   ```\n     640\n   \u00d7  70\n   ----\n   44800\n   ```\n\n4. **Multiply 640 by 200 (hundreds place):**\n   - Multiply 640 by 2: 640 \u00d7 2 = 1,280\n   - Add two zeros for the hundreds place: 128,000\n   ```\n     640\n   \u00d7 200\n   ----\n  128000\n   ```\n\n5. **Add All Partial Products:**\n   ```\n    1280\n  +44800\n  +128000\n  -------\n  174080\n   ```\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   The product of 640 and 272 is **174,080**.\n\n\\boxed{174080}",
