      "text": "188, 188.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 287 by 4, which gives me 1,148.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 287 by 50, resulting in 14,350.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 287 by 600, which equals 172,200.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 1,148 + 14,350 + 172,200.\n\nAdding them up, I get 187,698.\n\nSo, the correct product of 287 and 654 is 187,698.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 287 and 654 is \\boxed{187698}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 287 and 654, we can use the standard multiplication method. Here's a step-by-step breakdown:\n\n1. **Multiply 287 by 4 (the ones place of 654):**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 4 = 1,148\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 287 by 50 (the tens place of 654):**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 50 = 14,350\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 287 by 600 (the hundreds place of 654):**\n   \\[\n   287 \\times 600 = 172,200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1,148 + 14,350 + 172,200 = 187,698\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 287 and 654 is \\(\\boxed{187698}\\).",
