      "text": "133,125.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 355 by 5 (ones place of 375):**\n   - 5 \u00d7 5 = 25. Write down 5 and carry over 2.\n   - 5 \u00d7 5 = 25 + 2 = 27. Write down 7 and carry over 2.\n   - 5 \u00d7 3 = 15 + 2 = 17. Write down 17.\n   - **Partial Product:** 1,775\n\n2. **Multiply 355 by 70 (tens place of 375):**\n   - 70 \u00d7 5 = 350. Write down 0 and carry over 35.\n   - 70 \u00d7 5 = 350 + 35 = 385. Write down 5 and carry over 38.\n   - 70 \u00d7 3 = 210 + 38 = 248. Write down 248.\n   - **Partial Product:** 24,850\n\n3. **Multiply 355 by 300 (hundreds place of 375):**\n   - 300 \u00d7 5 = 1,500. Write down 00 and carry over 150.\n   - 300 \u00d7 5 = 1,500 + 150 = 1,650. Write down 50 and carry over 16.\n   - 300 \u00d7 3 = 900 + 16 = 916. Write down 916.\n   - **Partial Product:** 106,500\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   - 1,775 + 24,850 = 26,625\n   - 26,625 + 106,500 = 133,125\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 355 and 375 is \\boxed{133125}.",
