      "text": "200, 208.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me try again.\n\nFirst, I'll multiply 446 by 8, which gives me 3,568.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 446 by 40, resulting in 17,840.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 446 by 400, which equals 178,400.\n\nFinally, I'll add all these partial products together: 3,568 + 17,840 + 178,400.\n\nAdding them up, I get 200, 208.\n\nHmm, that still doesn't look correct. Maybe I made a mistake in my calculations. Let me check each step again.\n\nAfter rechecking, I realize that the correct sum should be 200, 208.\n\nWait, that still doesn't seem accurate. Perhaps I need to approach this differently.\n\nLet me try using the standard multiplication method.\n\nMultiplying 446 by 448:\n\nFirst, multiply 446 by 8: 446 \u00d7 8 = 3,568.\n\nNext, multiply 446 by 40: 446 \u00d7 40 = 17,840.\n\nThen, multiply 446 by 400: 446 \u00d7 400 = 178,400.\n\nNow, add all these partial products together:\n\n3,568 + 17,840 = 21,408.\n\n21,408 + 178,400 = 200, 208.\n\nWait, that still doesn't seem right. I think I might have made an error in adding the numbers.\n\nLet me add them again:\n\n3,568 + 17,840 = 21,408.\n\n21,408 + 178,400 = 200, 208.\n\nHmm, I'm getting the same result, but I'm not confident it's correct. Maybe I should use a different method, like the distributive property.\n\nLet's try that:\n\n446 \u00d7 448 = 446 \u00d7 (400 + 40 + 8) = 446 \u00d7 400 + 446 \u00d7 40 + 446 \u00d7 8.\n\nCalculating each part:\n\n446 \u00d7 400 = 178,400.\n\n446 \u00d7 40 = 17,840.\n\n446 \u00d7 8 = 3,568.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n178,400 + 17,840 = 196,240.\n\n196,240 + 3,568 = 199,808.\n\nAh, that makes more sense. So, the correct product is 199,808.\n\nI must have made a mistake in my initial addition. It's important to double-check each step to ensure accuracy.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 446 and 448 is \\boxed{199808}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 446 and 448, we can use the standard multiplication method by breaking down the multiplication into partial products and then summing them up.\n\n1. **Multiply 446 by 8:**\n   \\[\n   446 \\times 8 = 3568\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 446 by 40:**\n   \\[\n   446 \\times 40 = 17840\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 446 by 400:**\n   \\[\n   446 \\times 400 = 178400\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   3568 + 17840 + 178400 = 199808\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the product of 446 and 448 is \\(\\boxed{199808}\\).",
