      "text": "311,676.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 372 by 8 (ones place of 838):**\n   - 2 \u00d7 8 = 16. Write down 6 and carry over 1.\n   - 7 \u00d7 8 = 56, plus the carried 1 equals 57. Write down 7 and carry over 5.\n   - 3 \u00d7 8 = 24, plus the carried 5 equals 29. Write down 29.\n   - **Partial Product:** 2,976\n\n2. **Multiply 372 by 30 (tens place of 838):**\n   - 2 \u00d7 3 = 6. Write down 6.\n   - 7 \u00d7 3 = 21. Write down 1 and carry over 2.\n   - 3 \u00d7 3 = 9, plus the carried 2 equals 11. Write down 11.\n   - **Partial Product:** 11,160 (shifted one position to the left)\n\n3. **Multiply 372 by 800 (hundreds place of 838):**\n   - 2 \u00d7 8 = 16. Write down 16.\n   - 7 \u00d7 8 = 56. Write down 56.\n   - 3 \u00d7 8 = 24. Write down 24.\n   - **Partial Product:** 297,600 (shifted two positions to the left)\n\n4. **Add all partial products together:**\n   - 2,976 + 11,160 = 14,136\n   - 14,136 + 297,600 = 311,676\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 372 and 838 is \\boxed{311676}.",
