  "choices": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "110,500.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Write the numbers vertically aligned by place value:**\n   \n   ```\n     850\n   \u00d7 130\n   ```\n\n2. **Multiply 850 by 0 (the ones place of 130):**\n   \n   ```\n     850\n   \u00d7  0\n   ----\n     000\n   ```\n\n3. **Multiply 850 by 30 (the tens place of 130):**\n   \n   - Multiply 850 by 3: \\(850 \\times 3 = 2550\\)\n   - Since 30 is in the tens place, add a zero to the end: \\(25500\\)\n   \n   ```\n     850\n   \u00d7 30\n   ----\n   25500\n   ```\n\n4. **Multiply 850 by 100 (the hundreds place of 130):**\n   \n   - Multiply 850 by 1: \\(850 \\times 1 = 850\\)\n   - Since 100 is in the hundreds place, add two zeros to the end: \\(85000\\)\n   \n   ```\n     850\n   \u00d7100\n   ----\n   85000\n   ```\n\n5. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \n   ```\n     000\n   +25500\n   +85000\n   ----\n   110500\n   ```\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   The product of 850 and 130 is **110,500**.\n\n\\boxed{110500}",
