      "text": "100,000.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 112 by 9 (ones place):**\n   - 112 \u00d7 9 = 1,008\n\n2. **Multiply 112 by 80 (tens place):**\n   - 112 \u00d7 80 = 8,960\n\n3. **Multiply 112 by 800 (hundreds place):**\n   - 112 \u00d7 800 = 89,600\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   - 1,008 + 8,960 + 89,600 = 100,000\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 112 and 889 is \\boxed{100000}.",
